<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mendoza, Argentina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mendoza is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> at the foot of the Andes, the capital of Mendoza Province. Founded from Chile in 1561, it belonged to the Captaincy General of Chile until 1776. In 1814–1817 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-the-andes">Army of the Andes</a> there, with Chilean exiles, for the crossing that freed Chile. It is the centre of Argentina's wine industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mendoza-argentina.jpg" alt="Mendoza, Argentina" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CavernSaga · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Mendoza.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
